{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow women with serious illnesses to pause and resume maternity leave",
        "additional_details": "Pregnancy-associated cancer affects roughly 1 in 1,000 pregnancies. Mothers may miss time with their children due to hospital appointments, cancer treatments and recovery from side effects. Women may also face financial hardship as they cannot move to sick pay and then return to their maternity leave, particularly where sick pay is more generous than maternity pay. Ireland allows maternity leave to be paused for serious illness, and we want similar rights here.",
        "background": "Change the law to allow women diagnosed with cancer or another serious illness to pause and resume their maternity leave, as is possible in Ireland. Women should be able to take sick leave during this period and receive sick pay where eligible.",
